    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x,y)=(100,100),(12500,4),(800,25),(100000,1)$.\n\nEquate prime exponents: $2a+3c=10$ and $2b+3d=10$. Each has the two non-negative integer solutions $(5,0)$ and $(2,2)$.",
      "worked": "Write $x=2^a5^b$ and $y=2^c5^d$, where $a,b,c,d$ are non-negative integers. No other primes can divide $x$ or $y$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(2^a5^b)^2(2^c5^d)^3&=10^{10}\\\\2^{2a+3c}5^{2b+3d}&=2^{10}5^{10}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nUnique prime factorisation gives\n$$\\begin{align*}2a+3c&=10\\\\2b+3d&=10.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $0\\le c\\le3$ and $c$ must be even, $c=0$ or $2$. Thus $(a,c)=(5,0)$ or $(2,2)$. Similarly, $(b,d)=(5,0)$ or $(2,2)$.\n\nCombining these choices gives\n$$\\begin{align*}(a,b,c,d)&=(5,5,0,0),\\ (5,2,0,2),\\\\(a,b,c,d)&=(2,5,2,0),\\ (2,2,2,2).\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore all solutions are\n$$\\begin{aligned}(x,y)&=(100000,1),(800,25),\\\\(x,y)&=(12500,4),(100,100).\n\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 124
  },
